{
  "id": "statistical-conclusion-validity",
  "term": "statistical conclusion validity",
  "definition": "Statistical conclusion validity is the extent to which a study’s conclusions are supported by an appropriate analysis of its data. It depends on using statistical methods that fit the research question and give accurate results, especially in small samples, so that the findings are dependable rather than artifacts of poor analysis.",
